# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository.
#
# Added 2026-08-31, after commit 6446235 ("catchup") in appdaemon_wakeup_music
# rewrote every line of i1_wakeup_music.py as CRLF. The content was
# byte-identical -- verified by comparing both blobs with \r stripped -- but
# the diff read as 1445 insertions and 1445 deletions. That makes review
# impossible, and would have concealed a real change had one been mixed in.
# Backlog tickets T-20..T-29 cite line numbers in that file, so the risk was
# concrete. appdaemon_automatic_lights had drifted the same way, 912 lines.
#
# Most repos carrying this file were clean when it was added. It is here so
# they stay that way: the cause was an editor on another machine, and that
# machine will be used again.
#
# text=auto lets git detect which files are text; eol=lf pins the
# working-tree ending so CRLF cannot be reintroduced.
#
# Keep this file identical across every app repo, so that a diff between any
# two of them means something. Enforced by tests/test_line_endings.py.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats are never normalised. These carry incidental \r\n byte pairs
# that a text pass would corrupt.
*.parquet binary
*.joblib  binary
*.pyc     binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
